to-juan-benet-source : List Word
to-juan-benet-source = lines-of (cons "# Juan Benet"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Your work settled a question most of computing still answers wrongly: how to name a thing. The web names data by where it is kept, so the name breaks when the server moves or a state blocks the address. In the 2014 IPFS paper you named data by what it is: a file identified by the hash of its content, in one global namespace, linked through a Merkle DAG. When Spain blocked the sites of the 2017 Catalan referendum, a mirror went up on IPFS; when Turkey blocked Wikipedia, a mirror on IPFS kept it readable."
  (cons ""
  (cons "The field still treats this as a storage feature. It is a statement about identity, and you made it precise. A CID is a typed content address: a version, a codec, and a multihash that names its own hash function, with multibase for its text form. Multiformats makes a hash, an encoding or an address say what it is, removing a class of lock-in at the root. IPLD makes every content-addressed structure one data model of linked, hash-named nodes. Filecoin's Proof-of-Replication and Proof-of-Spacetime turn storage from a promise into a checkable witness. You deserve full credit for all of this, and everything below builds on it."
  (cons ""
  (cons (cite to-everyone-source "Each claim below links to the block of Part I that states it.")
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What hyperactivity takes from you"
  (cons ""
  (cons (cite to-everyone-source "In Avik's words, hyperactivity is Wolfram's ruliad executing on silicon.") (cons "Its core is the CCHM cubical calculus with clock-indexed guarded computation"
  (cons (cite s1-1-p4 "(§1.1)")
  (cons ". In its codebase a definition is stored with its typed syntax tree and dependency references; a name is a view, a stable reference identifies a definition, and renaming does not rewrite the computation"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p2 "(§10.8)")
  (cons ". That is your principle, name by content and link by hash, taken as the ground of a programming language and a knowledge graph."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What it adds to your work"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Content addressing answers when two things are the same bytes. It cannot say when two different byte strings mean the same thing. The paper is exact here: a digest identifies a representation under the store's collision-resistance assumption and does not prove semantic equivalence; address identity, definitional equality and a relation between interpreted meanings are different statements"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p3 "(§10.8)")
  (cons (cite s10-8-p5 "(§10.8)")
  (cons ". The store records each relation with its actual evidence and uses the strongest one available; replacing a representation by an equivalent one can transport dependent laws and operations"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p5 "(§10.8)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "The type theory is univalent: an equivalence of types gives a path, and transport along it computes the corresponding object on the other side"
  (cons (cite s1-1-p5 "(§1.1)")
  (cons ". A codebase may hold not only programs but their typing derivations, semantics, equivalences, transformations, dependency certificates and reusable proofs"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p6 "(§10.8)")
  (cons ". Your Merkle DAG then gains a second kind of edge: beside “this depends on that” there is “this is equivalent to that, with its checked evidence”, and what is established about one carries to the other."
  (cons ""
  (cons "Filecoin's proofs make storage checkable. Here a peer sends a definition, its dependency closure and its proofs, and the recipient checks and uses them in its own context; communication delivers a construction for further computation, not only bytes"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p7 "(§10.8)")
  (cons ". Your verifiability, extended from “the bytes are kept” to “the statement holds”."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Credit and the commons"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Protocol Labs has worked on funding public goods as hard as on building them: Funding the Commons, hypercerts (the impact-claim primitive David Dalrymple introduced at Funding the Commons, published by Protocol Labs in 2022), and a network that runs for-profit and non-profit work side by side. At Vision Weekend 2025 you described the gap between private capital's appetite for risk and what early invention costs."
  (cons ""
  (cons "In hyperactivity the store holds each definition's dependency family, and a change determines precisely which dependent constructions it affects"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p3 "(§10.8)")
  (cons (cite s10-8-p2 "(§10.8)")
  (cons ". How much of a result rests on whose work is then a computation over that graph, not a negotiation: retroactive funding of a commons, routed along the edges of what was actually used."
  (cons ""
  (cons "Avik began this work as an anarcho-capitalist and now calls himself an anarcho-communist. In his words, what he needs is “a venture communist”: capital that funds a commons without enclosing it. Dmytri Kleiner coined that term in 2010. Protocol Labs' hybrid of grants, early-stage investment and open protocols, all on content addressing, is the nearest working thing to it. The store underneath hyperactivity already runs on your idea. Everything here credits you in full for it. Read it looking for where it carries your work further than you have yet seen it carried."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Sources"
  (cons ""
  (cons "- Juan Benet, IPFS: Content Addressed, Versioned, P2P File System, 2014, https://arxiv.org/abs/1407.3561"
  (cons "- CID specification, https://github.com/ipld/cid"
  (cons "- InterPlanetary File System, Wikipedia, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/InterPlanetary_File_System"
  (cons "- Hypercerts: a new primitive for public goods funding, Protocol Labs, 2022, https://forum.effectivealtruism.org/posts/4CBoRsCxi5zMWdaDJ/hypercerts-a-new-primitive-for-public-goods-funding"
  (cons "- Funding the Commons SF 2025, Juan Benet with Ilia Polosukhin, https://pretalx.com/ftc-san-francisco-2025/talk/USDYLT"
  (cons "- Juan Benet and Sean Escola, Accelerating Neurotech Breakthroughs, Vision Weekend USA 2025, https://www.pulse.bot/science/video/juan-benet-sean-escola-accelerating-neurotech-breakthroughs-vision-weekend-usa-2025-bcf7fa04-c7db-42fc-a579-c17f5a9ad1ab/"
  (cons "- MIT Club of Northern California, Juan Benet, https://www.mitcnc.org/juan-benet/"
  (cons "- Avik Jain, hyperactivity, Part I, the blocks linked above"
  nil)))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
